This file is a PLACEHOLDER. It is not a key and will not verify anything.

To fetch the real UIDAI Offline eKYC signing certificate:

    curl -O https://uidai.gov.in/images/uidai_offline_publickey_26022019.cer
    openssl x509 -in uidai_offline_publickey_26022019.cer -pubkey -noout \
        > test-data/uidai_public_key.pem

The citizen portal reads this key to check the XMLDSig signature on an Offline
eKYC XML before it will build a proof. Without it the portal runs in DEMO mode:
it accepts synthetic XMLs, marks them `signature_valid = 1`, and stamps every
resulting proof bundle with `"demo": true` so no verifier can mistake a demo
proof for a real one.

See docs/UIDAI_INTEGRATION.md for how the real signature check binds to the
circuit's `signature_valid` signal, and for why that binding is the one part of
this prototype that a production deployment must harden.
